Now, a port of the parts of Python's statistics module that fit Thing: mean, median, mode, multimode, variance, stdev, covariance and correlation.
Now, use it from another program with outsource "statistics.thing", then call each one as Do mean(xs) and so on.
Next, a built-in square root, a way to raise an error, and number keys for a Book would remove the workarounds below.

Create sqrt(v),
    Now, Newton's method, since Thing has no square root yet.
    if v is smaller-than 0, give nil.
    if v is 0, give 0.
    A guess holds v.
    for every step in range(80), guess holds (guess + v / guess) / 2.
    give guess!

Create mean(xs),
    if Counted(xs) is 0, say("mean needs at least one number"), give nil.
    give Total(xs) / Counted(xs)!

Create median(xs),
    if Counted(xs) is 0, say("median needs at least one number"), give nil.
    A ordered holds Order(xs).
    A n holds Counted(ordered).
    if n % 2 is 1, give ordered[(n - 1) / 2].
    give (ordered[n / 2 - 1] + ordered[n / 2]) / 2!

Create counts_of(xs),
    Now, a Book is named with words, so each value is counted under its text.
    Book-of counts.
    for every x in xs, A key holds "{x}", if key in counts, counts[key] holds counts[key] + 1, if-not counts[key] holds 1.
    give counts!

Create multimode(xs),
    Now, every value that appears most often, in the order it first appears.
    List-of out.
    if Counted(xs) is 0, give out.
    A counts holds Do counts_of(xs).
    A best holds Bigger(counts).
    Book-of seen.
    for every x in xs, A key holds "{x}", if counts[key] is best and not key in seen, append(out, x), seen[key] holds Yes.
    give out!

Create mode(xs),
    if Counted(xs) is 0, say("mode needs at least one value"), give nil.
    give Do multimode(xs):0!

Create pvariance(xs),
    if Counted(xs) is 0, say("pvariance needs at least one number"), give nil.
    A m holds Do mean(xs).
    A total holds 0.
    for every x in xs, total holds total + (x - m) * (x - m).
    give total / Counted(xs)!

Create variance(xs),
    if Counted(xs) is smaller-than 2, say("variance needs at least two numbers"), give nil.
    A m holds Do mean(xs).
    A total holds 0.
    for every x in xs, total holds total + (x - m) * (x - m).
    give total / (Counted(xs) - 1)!

Create pstdev(xs),
    A v holds Do pvariance(xs).
    if v is nil, give nil.
    give Do sqrt(v)!

Create stdev(xs),
    A v holds Do variance(xs).
    if v is nil, give nil.
    give Do sqrt(v)!

Create covariance(xs, ys),
    if Counted(xs) is not Counted(ys), say("covariance needs lists of the same length"), give nil.
    if Counted(xs) is smaller-than 2, say("covariance needs at least two pairs"), give nil.
    A mx holds Do mean(xs).
    A my holds Do mean(ys).
    A total holds 0.
    for every i in range(Counted(xs)), total holds total + (xs[i - 1] - mx) * (ys[i - 1] - my).
    give total / (Counted(xs) - 1)!

Create correlation(xs, ys),
    A cov holds Do covariance(xs, ys).
    if cov is nil, give nil.
    A sx holds Do stdev(xs).
    A sy holds Do stdev(ys).
    if sx is 0 or sy is 0, say("correlation needs numbers that are not all the same"), give nil.
    give cov / (sx * sy)!
